# The Dockerfile copies only `requirements.txt` and `app/`, but everything else in this
# directory is still uploaded to the daemon as build context — 315 MB of it, almost all
# `.venv`. Excluding it takes the context to a couple of megabytes.
#
# The second reason is safety: `.env` and `serviceAccount.json` are real credentials
# sitting next to the Dockerfile. Nothing copies them today, but a future `COPY . .`
# would bake them into a pushed image. This makes that impossible rather than unlikely.

# ── credentials — never in an image ───────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
serviceAccount.json
*.pem
*.key

# ── local environments and caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── not needed at runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/
scripts/
spikes/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md

# ── editor and VCS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
